Ember: split-lock detection off by default

In its default "warn" mode the kernel also slows a program that takes a
split lock down on purpose. The programs that still do are mostly older
Windows games under Proton; split_lock_detect=warn turns it back on.

--- a/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/bus_lock.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/bus_lock.c
@@ -110,7 +110,12 @@
 
 static void __init sld_state_setup(void)
 {
-	enum split_lock_detect_state state = sld_warn;
+	/*
+	 * Ember: off unless asked for (split_lock_detect=warn). Warning about a
+	 * split lock also slows the program down on purpose, and the programs
+	 * that still take them are mostly older Windows games under Proton.
+	 */
+	enum split_lock_detect_state state = sld_off;
 	char arg[20];
 	int i, ret;
 
